※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4214 LANG_TYPE_ANSWER_DOES_NOT_FIT
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4215 LANG_TYPE_DIVISION_BY_ZERO

※ A program that must stop whenever it is started need not be built, so an
※ operation written down with both its operands and no answer that is a finite
※ number is reported where it is written rather than left to fault.  The same
※ rule the integers get, and for the same reason.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    @[ignore(5005)]
    1f64 ÷ 0f64
    @[ignore(5005)]
    1e308f64 × 10f64
    @[ignore(5005)]
    ⁻1e308f64 - 1e308f64
    0u6
